      "sub_type": "flat",
      "text": "Mr. Peanut (properly named Bartholomew Richard Fitzgerald-Smythe ) is the iconic anthropomorphic Mr. Peanut mascot and advertising logo for the Planters snack-food brand. Origin: He was created in 1916 by 14-year-old Antonio Gentile as part of a student design contest held by the Planters Nut and Chocolate Company . The Look: Gentile’s original sketch was enhanced by a commercial artist who added his signature top hat, monocle, cane, spats, and white gloves to give him the appearance of an old-fashioned gentleman. Identity: He is traditionally characterized as having British heritage and a refined demeanor.",
      "title": null,
      "type": "ai_overview",
      "url": null
    },
